 <p><strong>Question to investigate:</strong> Can students confirm that a particular food item is available without leaving Maps or contacting the restaurant?</p>
 <p><strong>Possible DineCheck advantage:</strong> Staff-confirmed campus item availability presented alongside dining hours and visible update times. A campus-specific workflow could help students decide where to eat between classes, but this advantage still needs testing.</p>
 <p><strong>Where DineCheck falls short:</strong> DineCheck’s proposed scope covers campus dining locations. Google Maps supports a broader search for restaurants on and off campus and combines discovery with directions and reviews. DineCheck has also not yet demonstrated a dependable process for keeping item availability current.</p>
